      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>The Minhag Polin (Eastern Ashkenazi) yotser (piyyut inserted into the beginning of the first blessing of the Shema service) for Shabbat haGadol, by the Sefaradi sage and paytan Joseph ibn Abitur. Translated with preserved acrostic and rhyme scheme. This piyyut juxtaposes the seven days of creation with the miracles of the Exodus as well as the promised future salvation in a three-by-three structure.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_66789_introduction"/>
